  m_text: '- Some people feel motion sickness, dizziness, nausea or eye strain in
    virtual reality. If you feel any discomfort, stop playing and rest until you
    feel completely fine.


    - A very small number of people may have seizures
    or blackouts triggered by flashing lights or patterns, even with no history of
    them. If you or anyone in your family has had epilepsy, talk to a doctor before
    playing. Stop right away if you notice twitching, blurred vision or confusion.


    -
    Clear your play area of furniture, people and pets, and stay inside your boundary.


    -
    Take a 10 to 15 minute break at least every 30 minutes. Don''t play when you
    are tired or unwell.


    - Children should play with an adult nearby.'
